    "classification-edge.md": {
      "note": "Raw-scan vs marked-token behaviour. Line 16 (`4.`) matches neither scanner (no content after the dot) and is absent from both. Line 17 (`5. [no-hooks]`) is marker-only: classifyLines still reports section-step (the editor paints what looks like a step, as it does today for main-flow marker-only lines) but BOTH the CLI parser and extractSections CULL it per contract 3.1 — hence its absence from expectedSections. Line 15 is a NO-divergence control: the marker regex is anchored so `**[no-hooks]**` is not stripped by the raw scan, AND extractPlainText is the identity in a tight list, so both passes agree byte for byte. Line 20 (numbered line inside a fenced block) is the SOLE genuine divergence — invisible to marked, a step to the raw scan — so this sectioned file must throw the CLI equal-lengths assert rather than warn-and-trim.",
